### Root Cause: Fundamental Scope Mismatch

The properties PROP-0031 through PROP-0044 were generated from specifications describing the **Execution Layer (EL) Patricia Merkle Trie** — specifically Python-like functions: `patricialize()`, `encode_node()`, `_prepare_trie()`, `root()`, `trie_set()`, `trie_get()`, `BranchNode`, secured/unsecured tries. These functions exist in the Python EL execution client or go-ethereum, **not in Prysm**.

Phase 02c's code resolution (`resolution_method: "grep_fallback"`) incorrectly mapped all 10 items to `BeaconState.HashTreeRoot` in `/home/gohan/runners/security-agent-1/_work/security-agent/security-agent/target_workspace/beacon-chain/state/state-native/state_trie.go` (lines 897-910), which is the **SSZ (Simple Serialize) Merkle tree** root computation for the CL beacon state — a fundamentally different data structure, algorithm, and protocol layer.

### Evidence

1. The file `beacon-chain/state/state-native/state_trie.go` contains `BeaconState.HashTreeRoot` which calls `stateutil.Merkleize(fieldRoots)` — a binary Merkle tree over SSZ fields, not a Patricia trie.

2. A full-text search of the Prysm `target_workspace` confirmed zero occurrences of: `patricialize`, `encode_node`, `_prepare_trie`, `BranchNode` (as EL trie node), `trie_set`, `trie_get`, secured/unsecured trie, or any EL Patricia trie node type.

3. The only "merkle" code found was SSZ state Merkleization and a deposit snapshot Merkle tree — both CL concepts unrelated to EL Patricia tries.

### Per-Item Verdicts

| Check ID | Property | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| CHK-PROP-0031-001 | BranchNode 16 subnodes in patricialize | Out-of-scope (EL trie) |
| CHK-PROP-0032-001 | patricialize assertion on value types | Out-of-scope (EL trie) |
